|~ `::explanation`, the kind of what `explain` answers, the page `doc`
   reads for a value and the value itself, and what is declared under
   it: the verbs that read it.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence], [QSSLF#explain]. ~|

:explanation
  |~~ An explanation sets a value beside the page that explains it, the
      answer of `explain`: the cord from what a reader holds to the page
      that tells what it is, in one answer. A value is explained by the
      page of its kind, a name by its own page, and a failure `!|`
      caught by the page of its refusal, which tells how to repair the
      call.

      It prints as a map under its tag, the page under `:page` above the
      value under `:value`, `::explanation{:page … :value 42}` for
      `42 | explain`; `page` and `value` read its parts.
      ::link~(::any/explain | doc) ::link~(::error | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang/errors | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | wraps
        |~~ The page and the value, a map, which `page` and `value` read.
        ~~|
        ::map
    | holds :NotPageAndValueError
        |~~ An explanation is the map of a page, under `:page`, and the
            value it explains, under `:value`.
        ~~|
        ~(keys | eq #[:page :value])
    | proves :explainsAFailure
        |~~ An error explained is an `::explanation`. ~~|
        ~("x" | add 1 !| explain | tag | eq ::explanation)
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ An explanation is a map of its page and its value. ~~|
        ~(::explanation#5 !| tag | eq ::explanation/PayloadKindNotTakenError)
    | proves :NotPageAndValueError/refusesAMapOfNeither
        |~~ A map of no page and no value is no explanation. ~~|
        ~(::explanation{} !| tag | eq ::explanation/NotPageAndValueError)

:explanation/page
  |~~ Answers the page that explains what `explain` was asked of: of a
      name its own page, `::vec/count | explain | page`; of a value the
      page of its kind, `#[1] | explain | page` the page of sets; of an
      error the page of the refusal it carries, the procedure that
      repairs the call, `"x" | add 1 !| explain | page`, or the page of
      what refused, the verb or its input, where the refusal has none; and
      null for a name declared without a page. The subject is an explanation, what
      `explain` answers, so a map is refused, its key `:page` read by
      `/page`. `value` answers what was explained.
      ::link~(::any/explain | doc) ::link~(::explanation/value | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns
        |~~ The page that explains the value, null for a name without one.
        ~~|
        #[::doc ::null]
    | throws :SubjectNotExplanationError
        |~~ `page` reads what `explain` answers,
            `::vec/count | explain | page`; the key `:page` of a map is
            read by `/page`.
        ~~|
    | proves :ofANameIsItsOwn
        |~~ The page of a name is its own. ~~|
        ~(::vec/count | explain | page | eq (::vec/count | doc))
    | proves :ofAValueIsThePageOfItsKind
        |~~ The page of a value is the page of its kind. ~~|
        ~(#[1] | explain | page | eq (::set | doc))
    | proves :ofAnErrorIsThePageOfItsRefusal
        |~~ The page of an error is the page of the refusal that raised
            it.
        ~~|
        ~("x" | add 1 !| explain | page | eq (::number/add/SubjectNotNumberError | doc))
    | proves :ofARefusalWithoutAPageIsThePageOfWhatRefused
        |~~ A refusal with no page of its own is explained by the page of
            what refused.
        ~~|
        ~(::a | gt !| explain | page | eq (::any/gt/value | doc))
    | proves :isNullForANameWithoutOne
        |~~ A name declared without a page is explained by none. ~~|
        ~(:x 1 | ::x | explain | page | eq null)
    | proves :SubjectNotExplanationError/refusesAMap
        |~~ A map with a key `:page` is no explanation. ~~|
        ~({:page 1} | page
          !| get [~(tag) /actualTag] | eq [::explanation/page/SubjectNotExplanationError ::map])
    | impl ~(get /page)

:explanation/value
  |~~ Answers the value the explanation explains, `42 | explain | value`
      answering `42`, and of a name the name,
      `::vec/count | explain | value` answering `::vec/count`. An error
      explained answers at rest, as `!|` caught it, and `raise` raises it
      again. The subject is an explanation, so a map is refused, its key
      `:value` read by `/value`. `page` answers what explains the value.
      ::link~(::any/explain | doc) ::link~(::explanation/page | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns
        |~~ The value explained, of any kind, an error at rest among them.
        ~~|
        ::any
    | throws :SubjectNotExplanationError
        |~~ `value` reads what `explain` answers, `42 | explain | value`;
            the key `:value` of a map is read by `/value`.
        ~~|
    | proves :isTheValueExplained
        |~~ The value is the one explained. ~~|
        ~(42 | explain | value | eq 42)
    | proves :isTheNameOfAName
        |~~ A name explained answers the name. ~~|
        ~(::vec/count | explain | value | eq ::vec/count)
    | proves :holdsAnErrorAtRest
        |~~ An error explained is the error at rest `!|` caught. ~~|
        ~("x" | add 1 !| explain | value | get /actualTag | eq ::string)
    | proves :SubjectNotExplanationError/refusesAMap
        |~~ A map with a key `:value` is no explanation. ~~|
        ~({:value 1} | value
          !| get [~(tag) /actualTag] | eq [::explanation/value/SubjectNotExplanationError ::map])
    | impl ~(get /value)

